// Wave 2 piece N: Execute E2E demo. Instant-kills target if their hp
// is below threshold. Lowers to EffectOp::Execute{hp_threshold: 20.0}.
//
// Conditional-emit path: the verb's `when` clause gates on target.hp <
// threshold; on fire it emits a Defeated event the new ApplyDefeat
// chronicle drains via agents.set_alive(c, false). Distinct from the
// existing inline Defeated emit in ApplyDamage's hp<=0 branch — both
// idempotently set alive=false.
//
// `when target.hp < 20` exercises Wave 1.5#7 when-condition lowering
// — the predicate body is captured as verbatim source text into
// program.when_per_effect[0]. The .sim verb's own `when` clause
// hand-mirrors the same predicate (target.hp < config.combat.reap_threshold).
// Registry-driven predicate evaluation is later infrastructure.
//
// `in cone(45deg, 5.0)` exercises Wave 1.5#2 in-shape lowering with
// the canonical 2-arg shape — radius matches the .sim's range gate.
//
// `{ stun 1s }` exercises Wave 1.5#9 nested-effect lowering — the
// inner stmt is recursively lowered to EffectOp::Stun{duration_ticks:
// 10} and pushed into program.nested_per_effect[0]. The .sim's
// existing emit fires Defeated only; apply-handler dispatch for the
// nested op (fire-after-outer-resolves) is deferred infrastructure.

ability Reap {
    target: enemy
    range: 5.0
    cooldown: 2s
    hint: damage

    execute 20 in cone(45deg, 5.0) when target.hp < 20 [PHYSICAL: 100] { stun 1s }
}
